    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW23N1cZVA1k1j52YPJWeeLJF)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- **Base: `415-devonthink-browse-tags` (#415).** Merge #415 first; GitHub retargets this PR to `main` when #415 merges and its branch is deleted. Until then the diff shows only this PR's changes.\n- Stack: #414 → #415 → **this PR** (independent of #418, #419, #420, #421, which also build on #415).\n- If merged out of order (into `main` before #415): impossible, `sp-devonthink-tags` does not exist on `main` yet.\n- #441 (chapter keywords, based on `main`): no code overlap.\n  - #441 writes the chapter's BibTeX `keywords` into the *parent's DEVONthink record comment* and a `* Keywords in the book …` section at the bottom of the chapter's note.\n  - This PR writes the *DEVONthink tags* of a record into a `- keywords :: …` meta line in the first section. Different place, different source; neither reads the other's data.\n  - Same word \"keywords\", so the meta line is a mirror of tags only. Text conflicts expected only in the key map (`T` here; #441 uses `c`/`C`) and the Keys table.\n- #437 (crossref resolver, merged): used as is. A chapter with no record of its own tags its parent's record; this PR then leaves the chapter's note alone (see below).\n- After merging: nothing to retarget.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Request:** write the tags into the litnote `.org` too, as a meta key `keywords` with comma-separated values, searchable.\n- **What:** `sp-devonthink-tag-note` (`C-c k d t`) re-reads the record's tags after the change and writes `- keywords :: a, b, c` in the first section of the litnote (with `C-u` removal too). DEVONthink stays the source of truth; the line is a mirror, never read back.\n- **Format** (same on every write): `, ` between tags, DEVONthink's order, no repeats, a legacy comma-joined tag written as its parts, no tags → empty value (line stays).\n- **Searchable:**\n  - `rg -i '^- keywords ::.*value form' ~/notes/litnotes`\n  - it is a vulpea meta line like `pub-author`, written with `sp-litnotes-meta--put`, so `sp-vulpea-meta-order` and meta search see it.\n  - `sp-see-also` keyword handling concerns Org TODO keywords, not meta lines, so there is no interaction.\n- **New:** `C-c k d T` `sp-devonthink-keywords-sync` refreshes the line without changing tags; option `sp-devonthink-keywords-key` (default `\"keywords\"`, nil turns the mirror off).\n- **Crossref (#437):** a chapter without its own record tags the parent's record (after asking). Those tags are the book's, so the chapter's litnote is **not** written (\"Keywords line not written…\"); `T` refuses there too. Run `T` in the parent's litnote.\n- **Not mirrored:** records tagged from the browser (`t` action on several marked records) do not touch their litnotes; run `T` in each note afterwards.\n- Buffer is left unsaved, like other `sp-litnotes-meta` edits.\n- Docs: new \"Mirroring the tags in the litnote\" section in `sp-devonthink-tags.org` (bullets), intro, keys and testing notes updated; `.el` re-tangled; README row updated.\n- Tests: 19 ERT tests in `sp-devonthink-tags-test.el` pass on Emacs 29.3 (8 new: value format, add/replace/empty line, option nil, mirror reads the record, chapter skip, own-record check, sync refusal, tag-note mirrors); `sp-litnotes-meta` tests (68) still pass; tangle check clean for this module. `when-let*` style only. No CHANGELOG edit.\n- **Not tested against DEVONthink or the real vault.** The AppleScript was run in no PR of this stack; tags read back after `set tags of` and their order are assumed.\n\n## Manual testing\n\nMac, fish, `~/.config/emacs-modular`, DEVONthink open on `literature`, a litnote with its own record. Throw-away tag `test-tag-1`.\n\n- [ ] Check out: `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 443-devonthink-tags-litnote-keywords; git checkout 443-devonthink-tags-litnote-keywords`, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] Unit tests: `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; emacs -Q --batch -L libraries/modules/academic -L libraries/modules/funct -L libraries/modules/vulpea -l ert -l tests/sp-devonthink-tags-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` → 19 pass (add `-L` for other module folders if Emacs asks)\n- [ ] In a litnote: `C-c k d t`, tag `test-tag-1` → \"Added: 1 record changed\"; the first section now has `- keywords :: …` after the other meta lines, listing the record's tags; buffer modified, not saved\n- [ ] Same tag again with `C-u C-c k d t` → \"Removed\"; the line no longer lists it\n- [ ] Order and format: a record with several tags → `a, b, c`; order matches DEVONthink's inspector; no duplicates\n- [ ] Edit the line by hand, then `C-c k d T` → line rewritten from DEVONthink; DEVONthink unchanged\n- [ ] Search: `rg -i '^- keywords ::.*test-tag-1' ~/notes/litnotes` finds the note after saving; a vulpea meta search on `keywords` lists it\n- [ ] Chapter litnote (no own record, `crossref` parent with a record): `C-c k d t` asks about the parent's record; on `y` the message says the keywords line was not written and the note has no `keywords` line; `C-c k d T` says to sync in the parent's note\n- [ ] Parent's litnote: `C-c k d T` writes the book's tags\n- [ ] `(setq sp-devonthink-keywords-key nil)` then `C-c k d t` → tags change in DEVONthink, no line written\n- [ ] Regression: browser `t` action on marked records still tags them; `sp-devonthink-split-comma-tags` unchanged\n- [ ] Clean up: remove `test-tag-1` in DEVONthink; `git -C ~/notes restore .` if the vault is under git\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (`git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`; restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- Litnotes: delete the `- keywords :: …` lines you generated, or `git -C ~/notes restore .`.\n- DEVONthink: remove `test-tag-1` from the tag list.\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; no yadm steps.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCEGsz9MCS2JAVY6BT)_",
